{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you shall stone them with stones.</b> Scripture was stricter regarding the betrothed woman, making her punishment stoning, more than a married woman, because she had not yet tasted the taste of intercourse. And this is a halakhah — she committed illicit relations and blemished the honor of herself and her family, and there is more disgrace than with a married woman, who is already blemished. And regarding the man who lay with her: since her betrothed was expecting to take her in her virginity and to taste in her the taste of virginity, and this one came and preceded him and blemished her first." "<b>Because she did not cry out in the city.</b> This matter proves that she consented to the transgression, for she was not afraid lest he kill her if she cried out, since they were in the city."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:53.384836724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}